  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340734",
      "title": "Granular Data Fetching With Suspense",
      "lectureOrder": 164,
      "videoOrder": 152,
      "sourceHash": "a9221609ef204e4e9e8d95147ceb255691640938d4d0e7df9dea0c329ca19d71",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.3,
          "end": 1.5,
          "en": "Now at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.5,
          "end": 6.06,
          "en": "this application has some minor problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.06,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "Most importantly, if I select a month here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "we don't get any feedback initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 12.623,
          "en": "until the data is loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.623,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "which takes a while, and we got no feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 17.97,
          "en": "whilst we're waiting for the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "And that might be strange.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "Why are we getting no loading feedback when loading a month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 28.443,
          "en": "even though we of course have a parent loading JS file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.97,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "Well, we're not getting any feedback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "because when selecting a month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 38.1,
          "en": "we already are on that filter page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.1,
          "end": 41.91,
          "en": "and therefore NextJS does not swap it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 43.352,
          "en": "for the loading fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.352,
          "end": 45.42,
          "en": "since we already have some data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.42,
          "end": 47.28,
          "en": "We're just loading some new data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.28,
          "end": 49.68,
          "en": "but we already did load data before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 53.043,
          "en": "so it's not showing us that loading fallback again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 57.06,
          "en": "Now we can work around that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.06,
          "end": 60.42,
          "en": "by using a more granular approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.42,
          "end": 63.72,
          "en": "of showing a loading fallback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.72,
          "end": 67.35,
          "en": "an alternative to using the loading JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 70.652,
          "en": "which, you by the way, can always use as an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.652,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "not just in situations like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 75.36,
          "en": "And that alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 80.36,
          "en": "uses the suspense component that is provided by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.49,
          "end": 83.803,
          "en": "to tell NextJS in detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.803,
          "end": 87.84,
          "en": "for which kind of data we wanna wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.84,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "and under which circumstances",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 93.21000000000001,
          "en": "a loading fallback should be shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.21000000000001,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now, how can we use suspense for that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 98.85,
          "en": "Well, as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.85,
          "end": 101.25,
          "en": "we have to create a separate component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.25,
          "end": 103.56,
          "en": "and we can do that in a separate file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.56,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "or in the same file as this page component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 108.69,
          "en": "And here I'll just use that same file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.69,
          "end": 111.063,
          "en": "to keep those things together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 115.05,
          "en": "Now you can give this component any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.05,
          "end": 117.693,
          "en": "I'll name it FilteredNews.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.09,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "Now here in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "I'll of course get a props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 128.3,
          "en": "and I expect up to two props to be passed to this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 132.24,
          "en": "the selected year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 135,
          "en": "or maybe just year to keep it a bit shorter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "and the selected month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 139.263,
          "en": "though both might be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.37,
          "end": 144.66,
          "en": "And then in the end, I wanna move that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.66,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "where I get the news forward a year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "out of the filtered news page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 153.18,
          "en": "into the filtered news component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 155.79,
          "en": "And therefore this should become an async component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.79,
          "end": 157.05,
          "en": "which it can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.05,
          "end": 160.52100000000002,
          "en": "because all components, not just page components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 160.52100000000002,
          "end": 164.823,
          "en": "are server components by default in NextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 169.35,
          "en": "So I'll create that news variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.35,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "and then I check if we have a year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.12,
          "en": "and we don't have a month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.12,
          "end": 175.954,
          "en": "And in that case, I'll set my news to the news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.954,
          "end": 177.754,
          "en": "for a selected year,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.754,
          "end": 181.23,
          "en": "though it's no longer called selected year here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.23,
          "end": 182.763,
          "en": "but instead just year.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "Else if we have a year and a month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 192.41,
          "en": "So if we have both, news should be set equal to get news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.51,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "for a year and month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 197.463,
          "en": "and I pass both the year and the month to that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 201.78,
          "en": "So now with that, I'm fetching my news like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 206.4,
          "en": "and then I wanna output that news list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.4,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "just as I did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 211.44,
          "en": "So I'll actually grab this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.44,
          "end": 213.99,
          "en": "where I also render some fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.99,
          "end": 215.859,
          "en": "in case we don't have any news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.859,
          "end": 219.153,
          "en": "and I'll cut this and add this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 220.8,
          "end": 222.93,
          "en": "And then I can just return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.93,
          "end": 227.476,
          "en": "that news content here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.476,
          "end": 230.85,
          "en": "Now we should clean up the filtered news page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 232.71,
          "en": "And there I still wanna extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.71,
          "end": 234.72,
          "en": "the selected year and selected month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.72,
          "end": 237.97,
          "en": "but we no longer need the news variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 243.15,
          "en": "and we also won't populate it here therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.15,
          "end": 246.27,
          "en": "And I'll actually also improve this code a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.27,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "and not fetch the same information twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 252.417,
          "en": "But instead, I'll just fetch my available years here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.417,
          "end": 254.73,
          "en": "and then use that fetched value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.73,
          "end": 258.093,
          "en": "as a default value for my links like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.5,
          "end": 263.07,
          "en": "And I now don't wanna output the news content here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.07,
          "end": 267.48,
          "en": "but instead this newly added filtered news component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.48,
          "end": 269.25,
          "en": "to which we pass a year prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.25,
          "end": 271.98,
          "en": "which is set equal to selected year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.98,
          "end": 275.313,
          "en": "and a month prop, which is set equal to selected month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.31,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "Now with that alone, nothing would change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 284.43,
          "en": "If I now reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.43,
          "end": 287.31,
          "en": "we are still loading the data for a selected year",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.31,
          "end": 289.89,
          "en": "and I can load the data for a selected month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.89,
          "end": 293.673,
          "en": "but I still get no loading fallback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 294.63,
          "end": 298.92,
          "en": "But now that we outsourced this data fetching logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.92,
          "end": 302.4,
          "en": "where we fetched and use for a year or month",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 302.4,
          "end": 305.55,
          "en": "into a separate React Server component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 305.55,
          "end": 309.153,
          "en": "we can use that React suspense hook I mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 310.23,
          "end": 315.06,
          "en": "So for that, we now wrap suspense around the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 315.06,
          "end": 316.89,
          "en": "that does the data fetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316.89,
          "end": 321.67,
          "en": "for which we want to provide our own custom loading fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.16,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "and suspense must be imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 329.223,
          "en": "So you must import this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.93,
          "end": 333.9,
          "en": "And with it being wrapped around a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 333.9,
          "end": 335.15999999999997,
          "en": "that fetches data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.15999999999997,
          "end": 337.8,
          "en": "it will automatically register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.8,
          "end": 341.01,
          "en": "if that component is still fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 341.01,
          "end": 345.87,
          "en": "and it allows us to show a fallback whilst that's the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 345.87,
          "end": 350.87,
          "en": "So here I can then say loading news or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.90999999999997,
          "end": 354.09000000000003,
          "en": "And with that, we then have a very granular way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 354.09000000000003,
          "end": 358.8,
          "en": "of telling NextJS that a part of the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 358.8,
          "end": 361.35,
          "en": "should be replaced with a fallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 361.35,
          "end": 363.633,
          "en": "if that part is fetching data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.25,
          "end": 367.92,
          "en": "With loading.js, it's less granular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 367.92,
          "end": 369.96,
          "en": "There we're telling NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 369.96,
          "end": 373.848,
          "en": "that an entire component, the entire page component actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.848,
          "end": 378.36,
          "en": "should be replaced with that fallback if it's fetching data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.36,
          "end": 380.395,
          "en": "But if we're then just re fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 380.395,
          "end": 383.34,
          "en": "it will not be replaced again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.34,
          "end": 386.79,
          "en": "And if we want it to be more granular in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.79,
          "end": 390.45,
          "en": "we couldn't do it with a loading JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 390.45,
          "end": 392.46,
          "en": "but we can be very granular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 392.46,
          "end": 395.223,
          "en": "by defining our own suspense boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 396.12,
          "end": 398.1,
          "en": "And therefore, with this added now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.1,
          "end": 401.15999999999997,
          "en": "if I now reload, we got the same effect as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 401.15999999999997,
          "end": 402.65999999999997,
          "en": "but now you already see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 402.65999999999997,
          "end": 404.73,
          "en": "we got the loading use fallback here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.73,
          "end": 407.34000000000003,
          "en": "and if I now click on a month,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 407.34000000000003,
          "end": 410.97,
          "en": "we also see loading use here until the month appears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 410.97,
          "end": 412.44,
          "en": "Though, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 412.44,
          "end": 414.87,
          "en": "it actually still takes a short while",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 414.87,
          "end": 418.5,
          "en": "until we see that fallback after I clicked on a month.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 418.5,
          "end": 422.85,
